{
  "_README": "Seam guard for the differences between runs. The viewer (viewer/run-differences.js, the Steps differences review) and the PDD (normalization/pdd_export.py, section 4.1) implement one algorithm: the alignment key of a step (draft:<draft_key>, merge:<JSON array of draft_keys>, else label:<process_label of the name>), the folding of consecutive run steps that spell a merged reference step, the difference lines, and the stretches of a run left out of the analysis. Both viewer/run-differences.test.js and normalization/test/test_run_differences_golden.py read every case here: `run_keys` is the alignment keys of the run after folding, `expected` the difference lines of the run against the pattern run, in order. Steps are listed in time order and are all visible (hidden steps never reach either side). A case with `excluded_ranges` also gives `run_span` (the run's start and end) and `origin` (when the recording started): each range is cut to the run's span, the pattern steps inside a stretch are not Skipped, and the run says once, first, that part of it was left out, with the times since the recording started. Change a case only together with both implementations.",
  "version": 1,
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "an identical run has no differences",
      "pattern": [
        { "name": "Look up the order", "draft_key": "crm|Orders|Button:find" },
        { "name": "Save the order", "draft_key": "crm|Orders|Button:save" },
        { "name": "Send the confirmation", "draft_key": "mail|Compose|Button:send" }
      ],
      "run": [
        { "name": "Orders: Find", "draft_key": "crm|Orders|Button:find" },
        { "name": "Orders: Save", "draft_key": "crm|Orders|Button:save" },
        { "name": "Compose: Send", "draft_key": "mail|Compose|Button:send" }
      ],
      "run_keys": [
        "draft:crm|Orders|Button:find",
        "draft:crm|Orders|Button:save",
        "draft:mail|Compose|Button:send"
      ],
      "expected": []
    },
    {
      "name": "extra steps, one at the start of the run and one after a step",
      "pattern": [
        { "name": "Look up the order", "draft_key": "crm|Orders|Button:find" },
